#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175719 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1fb22de-94c2-51a9-803b-f2bd77bcb012" :knowledge-point/title "Identitying the Type of the Image of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "954c2d7b-19d8-584b-aeb5-0927c79e2a65" :question/math-academy-id "e-13332" :question/problem "Consider the standard matrices of three linear transformations shown below. Which of these transformations map $\\mathbb{R}^2$ onto a line?\n\n![](images/7c/7cf595d0c2334cd4698c29991e58184b9e33db3f65bb1e99e5ce0c54714a67b3.png)" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear transformation over $\\mathbb{R}^2$ with the standard matrix $T,$ we have the following:\n\n- $T$ maps $\\mathbb{R}^2$ onto $\\mathbb{R}^2$ if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=2,$ i.e., $T$ is nonsingular.\n\n- $T$ maps $\\mathbb{R}^2$ onto a line if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=1.$\n\n- $T$ maps $\\mathbb{R}^2$ onto $(0,0)$ if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=0,$ i.e., $T$ is the zero matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $T_1$ maps $\\mathbb{R}^2$ onto a line. Notice that the columns of $T_1$ are linearly dependent but it's not the zero matrix. So, $\\text{rank}(T_1)=1.$\n\n- $T_2$ maps $\\mathbb{R}^2$ onto $\\mathbb{R}^2.$ Indeed, $T_2$ is a nonsingular matrix, i.e. $\\text{rank}(T_2)=2.$\n\n- $T_3$ maps $\\mathbb{R}^2$ onto $(0,0)$ since $T_3$ is the zero matrix, i.e. $\\text{rank}(T_3)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$T_1$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175720 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176088 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "390ecc8f-2938-5466-b49b-964a67f79755" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the One-Dimensional Image of a Linear Transformation in the Cartesian Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "91058f47-ebdb-5a02-ba3d-de01a1912041" :question/math-academy-id "e-13333" :question/problem "Consider the standard matrix $T$ of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n![](images/7b/7b576374332b6a30e024643ca3398b1c04c742a9994346e01c1b1b99495e4677.png)\nFind the equation of the line that the transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ maps $\\mathbb{R}^2$ onto." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $T$ has proportional rows, yet $T$ is not the zero matrix. \n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{rank}(\\mathbf{T})=1$ and $\\mathbf{T}$ maps $\\mathbb{R}^2$ onto a line that passes through the origin.\n\nMoreover, the line must pass through the origin $(0,0)$ and the points $(6,2)$ and $(-9,-3),$ which are defined by the columns of $T.$ \n\nComputing the slope $m$ of this line, we get\n\n$$\nm = \\dfrac{-3-2}{-9-6} = \\dfrac13.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $\\mathbf{T}$ maps $\\mathbb{R}^2$ onto the line $y=\\dfrac13x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175721 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "dd98751e-7fbd-5afa-b7ad-725ec479c996" :question/math-academy-id "e-13334" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that maps $\\mathbb{R}^2$ onto the line $y=-5x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\langle -1, 5 \\rangle \\in \\text{Im}(\\mathbf{T})$\n\n- $\\textrm{Ker}(\\mathbf{T})=\\{0\\}$\n\n- $\\textrm{Im}(\\mathbf{T})=\\Bbb R^2$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ with the standard matrix $T$ is a one-dimensional line, then\n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(T) = \\textrm{rank}(\\mathbf{T}) = 1,\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the point $(-1,5)$ satisfies the equation of the line $y=-5x$ since $5=-5\\cdot (-1).$ Hence, \n\n$$\n\\langle -1, 5 \\rangle \\in \\textrm{Im}(\\mathbf{T}).\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\textrm{nullity}(T)=1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Ker}(\\mathbf{T}) \\neq \\{\\mathbf0\\}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false.  Since $\\textrm{rank}(\\mathbf{T})=1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Im}(\\mathbf{T}) \\neq \\Bbb R^2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1fb22de-94c2-51a9-803b-f2bd77bcb012" :knowledge-point/title "Identitying the Type of the Image of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c09df208-63ec-50e5-ae40-2d1b49910690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T_{2}$ and $T_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173867} {:answer/id #uuid "c474152f-6ff4-5d2e-a342-baf10be3b0c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173868} {:answer/id #uuid "3c5ea241-68cd-54bb-8e50-36ebd9adb3fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173869} {:answer/id #uuid "5e717a7a-3246-59b5-988c-e72e6875da9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173870} {:answer/id #uuid "6bab6ae7-6669-5850-9b1f-ee8bd247cb23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$T_{1}$ and $T_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173871}] :answer-field/id #uuid "dff6c919-be8a-5f13-bc6a-323d7a217ae2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173866}] :question/id #uuid "c56c149d-6734-5355-8f48-32ec1a8b06b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-111292" :question/problem "Consider the standard matrices of three linear transformations shown below. Which of the transformations map $R^{2}$ onto the whole of $R^{2}$?\n\n$T_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}, T_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, T_{3} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364824 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1fb22de-94c2-51a9-803b-f2bd77bcb012" :knowledge-point/title "Identitying the Type of the Image of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6707aa95-7385-5666-ab9f-8e517cb70b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364826} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b4b4fb-b2a1-5812-abfe-7f88606e3432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364827} {:answer/id #uuid "6e6543ba-9d3b-5c31-8a43-6c7e29ccd78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364828} {:answer/id #uuid "402790a6-f9c8-58d8-a4a3-1a3276b60907" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364829} {:answer/id #uuid "4f65e360-ba17-56ee-887e-97b83e8472a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1b4b4fb-b2a1-5812-abfe-7f88606e3432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364827} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d4cdb48-2c70-5c58-8179-52d11b0057e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d90171a1-3d85-53bd-8f39-df0500121339" :question/math-academy-id "q-111763" :question/problem "Consider the standard matrices of three linear transformations shown below. Which of the transformations map ${R}^{2}$ onto a line?\n\n$$\n{T}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,{T}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{T}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear transformation over ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ we have the following:\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto ${R}^{2}$ if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=2,$ i.e., $T$ is nonsingular.\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=1.$\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto $(0,0)$ if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=0,$ i.e., $T$ is the zero matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- ${T}_{1}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line. Notice that the columns of ${T}_{1}$ are linearly dependent but it's not the zero matrix. So, $\\text{rank}({T}_{1})=1.$\n\n- ${T}_{2}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto $(0,0)$ since ${T}_{2}$ is the zero matrix, i.e. $\\text{rank}({T}_{2})=0.$\n\n- ${T}_{3}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto ${R}^{2}.$ Indeed, ${T}_{3}$ is a nonsingular matrix, i.e. $\\text{rank}({T}_{3})=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364831 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1fb22de-94c2-51a9-803b-f2bd77bcb012" :knowledge-point/title "Identitying the Type of the Image of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1193323c-44fb-5572-a466-a48f0837b06b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364833} {:answer/id #uuid "de034ae9-76ad-5215-a36e-e52af3f62552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364834} {:answer/id #uuid "d5d569b1-736f-58f8-be35-9701590fa377" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364835} {:answer/id #uuid "bd55cf8a-7800-58fa-a854-6cf5a91144d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364836} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b4e81e-8c58-5482-92db-3ddca0584936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd55cf8a-7800-58fa-a854-6cf5a91144d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364836} :answer-field/id #uuid "75355970-e9c5-5b8e-8c1c-20107867acd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f06b739-cec9-598b-8631-5e17e2f8f8d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-111767" :question/problem "Consider the standard matrices of three linear transformations shown below. Which of the transformations map ${R}^{2}$ onto a line?\n\n$$\n{T}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{T}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{T}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear transformation over ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ we have the following:\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto ${R}^{2}$ if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=2,$ i.e., $T$ is nonsingular.\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=1.$\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto $(0,0)$ if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=0,$ i.e., $T$ is the zero matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- ${T}_{1}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto $(0,0)$ since ${T}_{1}$ is the zero matrix, i.e. $\\text{rank}({T}_{1})=0.$\n\n- ${T}_{2}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line. Notice that the columns of ${T}_{2}$ are linearly dependent but it's not the zero matrix. So, $\\text{rank}({T}_{2})=1.$\n\n- ${T}_{3}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line. Notice that the columns of ${T}_{3}$ are linearly dependent but it's not the zero matrix. So, $\\text{rank}({T}_{3})=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1fb22de-94c2-51a9-803b-f2bd77bcb012" :knowledge-point/title "Identitying the Type of the Image of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d9dd698-468d-5fb9-8d32-a8bc2eb8d827" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364840} {:answer/id #uuid "0ce12a87-971f-5b50-bd6a-1d7d31b630d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364841} {:answer/id #uuid "c26f9043-1e7b-5030-9607-f522b18ea7ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364842} {:answer/id #uuid "3d39b4d3-3a29-5c85-a3e8-f6804fc1f612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364843} {:answer/id #uuid "b9118962-8fff-5461-a4b1-95a1ae553944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c26f9043-1e7b-5030-9607-f522b18ea7ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${T}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364842} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfbdeca3-4cba-5ac9-8012-e46807ec092b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364839}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a46963c9-d7c2-5857-8385-b98c37739cd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-111773" :question/problem "Consider the standard matrices of three linear transformations shown below. Which of the transformations map ${R}^{2}$ onto the whole of ${R}^{2}?$\n\n$$\n{T}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{T}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{T}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear transformation over ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ we have the following:\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto ${R}^{2}$ if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=2,$ i.e., $T$ is nonsingular.\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=1.$\n\n- $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto $(0,0)$ if and only if $\\text{rank}(T)=0,$ i.e., $T$ is the zero matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- ${T}_{1}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line. Notice that the columns of ${T}_{1}$ are linearly dependent but it's not the zero matrix. So, $\\text{rank}({T}_{1})=1.$\n\n- ${T}_{2}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto $(0,0)$ since ${T}_{2}$ is the zero matrix, i.e. $\\text{rank}({T}_{2})=0.$\n\n- ${T}_{3}$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto ${R}^{2}.$ Indeed, ${T}_{3}$ is a nonsingular matrix, i.e. $\\text{rank}({T}_{3})=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{3}$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec8c126b-beb0-5259-95a8-ee03317b9dbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477289} {:answer/id #uuid "05b4a708-dd67-557a-9e5d-3cec0dfaf56e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec8c126b-beb0-5259-95a8-ee03317b9dbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477289} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e9fdd20-93bb-54d2-8f45-dd434f374b95" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477614} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ca155e7-6b82-5264-aff3-a5b9bbf22322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477291} {:answer/id #uuid "d241b648-c419-53a1-bd11-5a4510ba9eba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ca155e7-6b82-5264-aff3-a5b9bbf22322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477291} :answer-field/id #uuid "8474779a-6aa5-57d6-8c8a-638b08fec6e2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477615} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85d7e293-6acb-57a3-84e4-89d7e0daf5c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477293} {:answer/id #uuid "c9be56df-604d-5bf1-b89a-a5381de8206d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9be56df-604d-5bf1-b89a-a5381de8206d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477294} :answer-field/id #uuid "6637f2a2-acef-52c2-99ff-897ed538dbfe" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477616}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4acbb26f-7e4b-53ce-a37d-bd74763516c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-38297" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ to the origin. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $\\text{rank}(T)=1$,  where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$\n- **II.** $\\text{Im}(T)$ contains no vectors of ${R}^{2}$\n- **III.** $\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $T$ in ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T$ is the zero-subspace ${0},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=0\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. In our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The image of $T$ contains the vector zero vector $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=2$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d07d408-4bd4-52a2-b369-1432edfe2c77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469020} {:answer/id #uuid "eaeb8c45-a223-54ca-b996-e4cc9a54fe8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d07d408-4bd4-52a2-b369-1432edfe2c77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469020} :answer-field/id #uuid "246b7ed5-a7fd-53be-80d4-b0d726f0fda5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f53549c-840d-53f3-bf45-f0d90bcc6ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469022} {:answer/id #uuid "215f631a-fd6a-5cc0-906f-13e0a5fbd25e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "215f631a-fd6a-5cc0-906f-13e0a5fbd25e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469023} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a6bf326-d27f-5130-ad2f-4b066b4f2754" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470123} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bb3b5e2-0da0-57b0-a807-697b0aeddec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469024} {:answer/id #uuid "a8fd395f-d3c4-53ed-b990-698626ffd03e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bb3b5e2-0da0-57b0-a807-697b0aeddec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469024} :answer-field/id #uuid "435f823d-9228-557b-a231-fc7e35bab06c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "34581764-4087-5b06-9eff-4679fe703405" :question/math-academy-id "q-38300" :question/problem "If the linear transformation $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto the line $y=-3x$ then, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨1,3⟩$ belongs to the range of $T$\n\n- **II.** $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}$\n\n- **III.** $\\text{Im}(T)={0}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $T$ in ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T$ is a one-dimensional line, then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=1\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. \nNotice that the point $(1,3)$ does not satisfy the equation of the line $y=-3x$ since $3\\ne -3\\cdot 1.$ Therefore, the vector $⟨1,3⟩\\notin \\text{Im}(T).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \nsince $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line passing through the origin, we have that the standard matrix $T$ is singular. Hence, $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. \nFor example,  the point $(1,-3)$ satisfies the equation  $y=-3x$ since $-3=-3\\cdot 1.$ Therefore, the vector $⟨1,-3⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T).$ Thus, $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {0}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366059 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf5d61a3-731b-5ca2-a21d-a258c3b1767d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469026} {:answer/id #uuid "83d5e69a-fb13-5cb4-8279-35f40cd14786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf5d61a3-731b-5ca2-a21d-a258c3b1767d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469026} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad7fbb88-7ce0-52f3-bfca-0238dcd3a81c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94b0ff15-d102-5f1d-af4e-e362a8a9b9a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469028} {:answer/id #uuid "c0529496-06cf-5552-ac7c-13815e3edd61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0529496-06cf-5552-ac7c-13815e3edd61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469029} :answer-field/id #uuid "990ff885-053e-5892-a630-17d9382e4120" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470126} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e46a229c-3d63-5185-b98f-3bcb74c8a528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469030} {:answer/id #uuid "c12af7cf-9477-5a53-a812-9a97f8176c74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e46a229c-3d63-5185-b98f-3bcb74c8a528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469030} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bce9e44-27f0-518d-ad2a-de5a2a028195" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "07bd3910-da00-5269-ba42-c4e894fc0a77" :question/math-academy-id "q-38305" :question/problem "If the linear transformation $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto the line $5y=6x$ then, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨\\frac{6}{5},1⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T)$\n\n- **II.** $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}$\n\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(T)=0$, where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $T$ in ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T$ is a one-dimensional line, then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=1\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false.\nNotice that the point $(\\frac{6}{5},1)$ does not satisfy the equation of the line $5y=6x$ since $5\\cdot 1\\ne \\frac{6}{5}\\cdot 6.$ Therefore, \n$⟨\\frac{6}{5},1⟩\\notin \\text{Im}(T).$\n\n- Statement II is true.\nSince $T$ maps ${R}^{2}$ onto a line passing through the origin, we have that the standard matrix $T$ is singular. So, $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}.$\n\n- Statement III is false.\nSince  statement II is true we have that $\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{dim(Ker}(T))\\ne 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12eb12db-c865-5a15-995f-57d1e99856b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452323} {:answer/id #uuid "fa2992f7-296f-52e8-8e2f-b1875fa14a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12eb12db-c865-5a15-995f-57d1e99856b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452323} :answer-field/id #uuid "12ebab7b-febe-5850-8be3-97869ab43f9b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453009} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dff232c6-f90e-549a-bf5d-1544c0d7eb35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452325} {:answer/id #uuid "cc22eb64-3d36-5f56-935a-3d6d0d508e49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc22eb64-3d36-5f56-935a-3d6d0d508e49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452326} :answer-field/id #uuid "9583cd23-de18-5d81-9215-33038a6df612" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453010} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d092dba5-3f4c-5126-93c1-b72bf8d37079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452327} {:answer/id #uuid "3d4acc6c-2043-51df-a00b-c80988412bef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d092dba5-3f4c-5126-93c1-b72bf8d37079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452327} :answer-field/id #uuid "5957978d-2e1f-5607-8d63-c7b81149356e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453011}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2335439b-17b4-5a3d-b1ce-91063205bf0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-97079" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ onto the line $y=2x.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $⟨2,1⟩\\in \\text{Im}(T)$\n- **II.** $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}$\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(T)=2$, where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $T$ in ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T$ is a one-dimensional line, then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=1,\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. The point $(2,1)$ does not satisfy the equation of the line $y=2x$ since $1\\ne 2\\cdot 2.$ Hence, \n\n$$\n⟨2,1⟩\\notin \\text{Im}(T).\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\text{nullity}(T)=1,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have that \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(T)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}]}
